	(text "1. Add CAN bus ports. Likely two? Alternatively RS485 or something.\n2. Ensure charger board connector is large enough to handle future expansion\n3. Ensure charger IO are 5v tolerant (bidirectional)\n4. Add RJ45 connectors to talk to multiple balancers\n5. Add RJ45 connectors to talk to multiple inverters\n6. Am I building a DCU + HID?\n7. Do I need to provision for a WiFi Connection? Maybe an ESP32 is a better choice for that.\n8. Would need IO between ESP32 and RP2040.\n9. Honestly at that point. Just put the RP2040 on the charger and have it talk RS485."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
